  "_SECURITY_NOTICE": "THIS FILE HAS BEEN NEUTRALIZED. The RSA private key that was here has been committed to git history and must be treated as compromised.",
  "_ACTION_REQUIRED": [
    "1. REVOKE the old key: treat any JWT signed with the old RSA key as untrusted. Invalidate all active sessions if this key was ever used for signing.",
    "2. GENERATE a new symmetric key for HMAC-SHA256: run `openssl rand -base64 64` (minimum 32 bytes / 256 bits) on your machine.",
    "3. SET the environment variable: add JWT_KEY=<your-new-key> to your .env file (which is already git-ignored) or your deployment secrets manager.",
    "4. DO NOT put any real key material back into this file. The app reads its signing key from the JWT_KEY environment variable (see Program.cs).",
    "5. This file is now listed in .gitignore. Keep it there."
